{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, דָּת","hw":"דָּת","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">דָּת</span></big>  <strong>n.f.</strong> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:9\" href=\"/Daniel.6.9\">Dn 6:9</a> <strong>decree, law (</strong>Syriac; Pers. loan-word, v. BH<strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ד׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:16\" href=\"/Daniel.6.16\">Dn 6:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:25\" href=\"/Daniel.7.25\">7:25</a>, cstr. <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:14\" href=\"/Ezra.7.14\">Ezr 7:14</a> +; emph. <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּתָא</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:12\" href=\"/Ezra.7.12\">Ezr 7:12</a> +; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּֽתְכוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:9\" href=\"/Daniel.2.9\">Dn 2:9</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>decree</em> of king <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:13\" href=\"/Daniel.2.13\">Dn 2:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:15\" href=\"/Daniel.2.15\">15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:26\" href=\"/Ezra.7.26\">Ezr 7:26</a>; c. sf. <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:9\" href=\"/Daniel.2.9\">Dn 2:9</a> <em>decree against you</em>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  unchangeable <em>law</em> of Medes and Pers. <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:9\" href=\"/Daniel.6.9\">Dn 6:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:13\" href=\"/Daniel.6.13\">13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:16\" href=\"/Daniel.6.16\">16</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  <em>law</em> of God (in mouth of non-Jews): <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:6\" href=\"/Daniel.6.6\">Dn 6:6</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:12\" href=\"/Ezra.7.12\">Ezr 7:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:14\" href=\"/Ezra.7.14\">14</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:21\" href=\"/Ezra.7.21\">21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:26\" href=\"/Ezra.7.26\">26</a>, so (abs.) <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:25\" href=\"/Daniel.7.25\">Dn 7:25</a>; <em>laws</em> of God <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:25\" href=\"/Ezra.7.25\">Ezr 7:25</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, דֶּ֫תֶא","prev":"BDB Aramaic, אֶדְרַע²"}